e pending in OutputFrameWorker, and not returned to framework immidiately.  This patch will return result of request immidiately if no postprocess is needed.  BUG=b:117760723 TEST=Build and deploy package to platform and camera works  Change-Id: Ic163b0e36374d36fe93d18449b42e30731141af8 Signed-off-by: Qingwu Zhang &lt;qingwu.zhang@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1298603 Commit-Ready: Wei Meng &lt;wei.meng@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Wei Meng &lt;wei.meng@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1298603" owner_email="wei.meng@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/arc-camera" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/arc-camera" ref="refs/changes/03/1298603/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I809e39a2899e002da52f01c3e59eee46cde55a13" commit="190e11bf2c5e40362c282ad5ca6887f707216bd5" commit_message="hal_adapter: Allow selectively disable cameras  Add &quot;enable_front_camera&quot;, &quot;enable_back_camera&quot;,     &quot;enable_external_camera&quot; options for selectively disable cameras in     cros_camera_service.  BUG=b:112621181 TEST=Set {&quot;enable_front_camera&quot;: false}, {&quot;enable_back_camera&quot;: false},     {&quot;enable_external_camera&quot;: false} to /run/camera/test_config.json     see if built-in camera app only detect available cameras.  Change-Id: I809e39a2899e002da52f01c3e59eee46cde55a13 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1168957 Commit-Ready: Kuo Jen Wei &lt;inker@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kuo Jen Wei &lt;inker@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shik Chen &lt;shik@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1168957" owner_email="inker@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="22" project="chromiumos/platform/arc-camera" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/arc-camera" ref="refs/changes/57/1168957/22" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I0b9a60dcede4ab447996915c252dcc306b811ea6" commit="8701459c039ef4fae9f7a4071a1af7d7d6c94e95" commit_message="BACKPORT: ath10k: add waiting htt tx complete before wow enable  If there are some tx packets pending in firmware, and then system enters suspend, firmware will fail for wow enable. This will trigger mac80211 to stop ath10k and download firmware again, then it is non-wow suspend.  After add the waiting htt tx complete, then firmware will have some time window to send or flush the pending tx packets.  Tested with QCA6174 PCI with firmware WLAN.RM.4.4.1-00109-QCARMSWPZ-1, but this will also affect QCA9377 PCI. It's not a regression with new firmware releases.  Signed-off-by: Wen Gong &lt;wgong@codeaurora.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Kalle Valo &lt;kvalo@codeaurora.org&gt;  (cherry picked from commit 828853ac58265c93249b53ba81782213962d5d4e) Conflicts:  drivers/net/wireless/ar10k/ath/ath10k/mac.c (comment style)  drivers/net/wireless/ar10k/ath/ath10k/mac.h (declaration context)  BUG=b:113962643 TEST=Test with tx traffic and do wow suspend success.  Change-Id: I0b9a60dcede4ab447996915c252dcc306b811ea6 Signed-off-by: Wen Gong &lt;wgong@codeaurora.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1205677 Commit-Ready: Wen Gong &lt;wgong@qti-qualcomm.corp-partner.google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1205677" owner_email="wgong@qti-qualcomm.corp-partner.google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/77/1205677/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><lkgm version="11209.0.0-rc5"/></manifest>